zune-jpeg: keep the up-sampler's carried-over rows when a scan resumes

`decode_mcu_ycbcr_baseline_inner` calls `set_upsampling()` on every
`decode_into` attempt, and that re-runs `Components::setup_upsample_scanline`,
which clears any buffer whose length differs from its computed size. The
horizontal up-sampler (worker.rs, `SampleRatios::H` in a vertically sampled
image) resizes `upsample_dest` to `2 * raw_coeff.len()` and keeps the last
up-sampled row of the previous MCU row in it for the next row's
`first_row_upsample_dest`. When an incremental decode resumed from an MCU-row
checkpoint, the setup zeroed that row, so the two output rows at the MCU-row
seam came out different from a one-shot decode ("incremental pixels diverge
from one-shot decode"). `set_upsampling` now takes `resuming` and skips the
buffer setup when the baseline scan resumes from a checkpoint (the buffers
are still the ones the earlier attempt set up); progressive rendering passes
false. Includes a regression test (tests/incremental_resume.rs).

Not fixed upstream as of zune-image 2cdbbf5.
Upstream: none found; open #514 (raw output allocates no upsampler buffers)
touches the same `set_upsampling` call sites.

diff --git a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs
index 61953f30..ef514de6 100644
--- a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/decoder.rs
@@ -4006,7 +4006,11 @@ where
     }
 
     /// Set up-sampling routines in case an image is down sampled
-    pub(crate) fn set_upsampling(&mut self) {
+    ///
+    /// `resuming` is true when a baseline scan resumes from an MCU-row
+    /// checkpoint: the rows the up-samplers carried over from the previous
+    /// MCU row are then still needed and must not be reset.
+    pub(crate) fn set_upsampling(&mut self, resuming: bool) {
         // no sampling, return early
         // check if horizontal max ==1
         if self.h_max == self.v_max && self.h_max == 1 {
@@ -4039,7 +4043,9 @@ where
                     generic_sampler()
                 }
             };
-            comp.setup_upsample_scanline();
+            if !resuming || comp.upsample_dest.is_empty() {
+                comp.setup_upsample_scanline();
+            }
             comp.up_sampler = samp_factor;
         }
     }
